# Pebbix licensing scope

Copyright (c) 2026 kr.donminzzi, except material with its own notices.
Pebbix is a mixed-license, source-available game.
The unmodified texts in LICENSES/ govern their respective material.
There is no repository-wide MIT grant for this revision.

## Default game software: PolyForm Noncommercial 1.0.0

Project-authored app code, game rules, presentation, session integration, game-specific tests, tools, and configuration use PolyForm Noncommercial 1.0.0.
This includes lib/game/domain/, components/, view/, widgets/, session/, and game-specific capture, preview, and store tools, subject to the exact exceptions below.
Use LICENSES/PolyForm-Noncommercial-1.0.0.txt, including its express permitted purposes and organization provisions.
Commercial reuse outside those permitted purposes, including paid or advertising-funded repackaging, requires separate permission from the relevant rights holders.
This summary does not change the license text.

## Exact MIT exceptions

Only these project-owned reusable source files are designated MIT:

- lib/game/cubit/audio/bounded_audio_pool.dart
- lib/loading/widgets/animated_progress_bar.dart
- tool/generate_special_shot_audio.py
- tool/postprocess_flutterfire.py
- tool/test_postprocess_flutterfire.py

The synthesized assets/audio/bomb.mp3 and assets/audio/rainbow.mp3 also remain MIT.
Retain LICENSES/MIT.txt and applicable copyright and source notices when reusing them.
Taking a fragment from another game file does not make it MIT.
There is no MIT OR noncommercial choice for the game body.
MIT components may be reused commercially, including in an independently created game.

## Original explanatory prose: CC BY 4.0

Project-authored README, development, architecture, planning, validation, and retrospective prose is CC BY 4.0.
Attribution and the other conditions in LICENSES/CC-BY-4.0.txt apply.
Embedded implementation snippets retain their source license: game snippets remain PolyForm Noncommercial and snippets from exact MIT exceptions remain MIT.
Images, video, quoted correspondence, and externally owned material are not relicensed as prose.
An unmarked game-code example is not automatically MIT.

## Original artwork and motion: CC BY-NC 4.0

Project-created game images, animation sources, and their derivatives are CC BY-NC 4.0, only to the extent the project holds licensable rights.
Use LICENSES/CC-BY-NC-4.0.txt.
This does not guarantee copyright protection or exclusivity for AI-generated material.
See BRAND_USAGE.md for official-affiliation representations.

## Third-party material and earlier grants

Five externally sourced audio files retain CC0-1.0; both Pretendard fonts retain OFL-1.1 and the original notice.
Template-derived portions and dependencies retain their original rights and notices; the game's noncommercial terms do not replace those terms for the materials themselves.
See THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md and REUSE.toml for paths and provenance.
Third-party quotations, including Apple review correspondence, receive no new license from this project.

These terms describe this revision and do not revoke permissions previously granted with earlier copies.
They do not prohibit independently written similar games or guarantee store acceptance.
Keep the development repository private and prepare a separately reviewed, history-free snapshot for AndrewDongminYoo/pebbix.
